/* Model-owned refinements/regions-and-bulk declarations; imported by shared-heap-smp.sysml. */
package GambitSharedHeapSmpRegionBulkRefinement {
 private import GambitSharedHeapSmp::*;

 part bulkRuntimeInterface:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="bulkRuntimeInterface";
  attribute :>> precondition="Held VM/operation lifetime precedes dereference; actual BULK/SFUN purpose, exact source/target attempt and input revision, fixed root layout, real data closure and protected membership qualify each private operation";
  attribute :>> argument="Existing setup core/result/postlude and RC source/lifecycle consumers are mapped to private operation contracts in the bound interface packet. Core completion, pending error and native cleanup are separate. Target prepare/install/query/ACK uses one held intent, valid typed writes, complete commit and future source coverage. Allocation-to-result-publication uncertainty is explicitly retained rather than hidden by metadata intent. Actual caller mapping preserves startup first_iter=0, ordinary sync first_iter=1, request-count decrement under TRY and legacy BOOL/SFUN result projection. Query call success is distinct from target commit state. Current registration exposes a linked-node prefix before domain/count stores complete, same-domain re-registration returns without repairing that prefix, and release_rc treats domain zero as private. Native allocator/debug counters provide no keyed result journal. Owned allocation capture must be separate from accepted borrowed roots in lifecycle records. The real begin_sfun success path installs procedure in a registered bank, acquires the bank loan, then returns the closure-self loan; failure separately releases an unborrowed bank. Marker revocation keeps bank/entry through physical END_SFUN. Registration witness must bind one held node/source/attempt and actual complete outcome, not stored domain/count observations alone. In the reviewed cooperative register_rc body, all ordinary refusal returns precede the first list write and no explicit Scheme poll/callback/throw occurs inside registration. Receipt issuance can follow qualified normal return instead of inventing interior recovery. Current marker prepare/abort now reuse or free a cleared IDLE record; new allocation/intent/query debts must be excluded from that reuse eligibility.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Runtime owner receives complete input/authority/linearization/result/custody/retirement contracts and a whole native acceptance set. Existing entry names and SFUN rules remain; proposed private helpers implement real responsibilities, not a parallel runtime/configuration/registry. No source/native closure is issued by this interface definition.";
  attribute :>> missing="Implement purpose-aware writer and lifecycle dispatch, synchronization core extraction and permitted postlude, one-intent target allocation/install/query/ACK, actual source/target lifetime and scan consumers. Prove native allocation result capture, lock order, first-error/root representation and old data closure; unknown OS/native outcomes remain retained where no recovery witness exists. Unify prepared-allocation versus accepted-loan settlement across begin_sfun failure, marker_abort, end_sfun and terminal close. Registration completion witness is proposed native metadata under existing handoff roles, not an existing runtime receipt or robust journal.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Exact operation keys and all partial/lost-return boundaries; real purpose/index/source checks, combined GC/control/effect ordering, overlap/movement/multi-shot semantics, stale helper/query, target commit/ACK and original owner exit before next W<R GC. Unchanged budgets and independent matched costs required. Include allocator-private/linked/returned-but-unadopted windows, typed parameter/range guards, all real sync callers and no-GC interval between source ACK/owner exit and next GC. Distinguish each abstract link-store prefix without assuming compiler/hardware visibility order; do not free reachable domain-zero nodes or return an unaccepted root loan. Query/ACK requires known registration/adoption and continuous target coverage, not matching shape/count. Cover permanent no-bank entry, closure-self transfer, partial root allocation, bank-loan rejection/lost result, marker allocation GC/failure, ACTIVE-to-REVOKED with physical call still live, nested call entry and all three cleanup consumers; ACK then actual old owner exit followed by W<R GC must retain exact target roots. Separate ordinary prewrite refusal and published-reply loss from out-of-contract interior native interruption. Extend actual IDLE eligibility and all reuse/free consumers before introducing pending allocation/intent/query state; zero visible root fields alone cannot establish it.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Existing QNT temporal and Lean data/slot/alias/accounting owners stay unchanged; C ABI/control/lifetime and actual producer/consumer adapters require source/native acceptance. Interface result vocabulary is not another formal state machine or proof.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A stale pointer cannot be made queryable by a generation field; lost allocation output cannot become known absence. ACK does not itself free source or authorize raw data access; waiting for next GC DONE can form an exit dependency. Holding a metadata/source gate across GC/callback creates a wait cycle.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeFailure;
  ref part :>> entrySite=bulkCoreOutcome;
  ref part :>> exitSite=bulkTargetScanChain;
 }
 part bulkSyncRootDelivery:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="bulkSyncRootDelivery";
  attribute :>> precondition="Bulk operation has complete canonical roots and closed physical spans; collective request identity, first pending error, owner cleanup state and installed target revision have separate lifetimes; no target/source retirement crosses an unqualified roster cut";
  attribute :>> argument="run_and_throw_error_on_processor_0 sends startup return through OP_PROCESSOR_0_THROW_ERROR. execute_sync_op_loop retains first error locally, completes collective arbitration and matching-request result delivery, calls lifecycle_drain and only then throws on processor0. release_foreign clears callback/payload before invocation; drain saves originals in an inflight record and marks uncertainty on failure. RC registration plus next root_round_begin/freeze/publish/strided scan/mark_rc supplies the actual target scan chain, not root_task_scan_vm over an arbitrary native list.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Separate core-memory/request completion from error/effect delivery while retaining current ordering and designated recipient. Target install ACK needs complete roots, stable source membership and protection in every overlapping/future GC prefix, not waiting for another GC to execute. Native cleanup, root transfer and next-round scan must compose as one adapter with exact outcome records.";
  attribute :>> missing="Implement pre-reserved/rooted pending state and purpose-aware ordinary versus effect-restricted postlude; distinguish nested drain, pending/inflight/uncertain outcomes and disallow replay. Provide target-purpose root writes, pinned deduplicated query/ACK, membership/source lifetime and next-round scan consumers. Actual current code has no such bulk source transfer/result service.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Combine multiple startup/control errors with cleanup pending/failure/nesting and lost core/result ACK; preserve first-error selection and designated delivery without hiding cleanup uncertainty. Cover target install before next cut, overlapping-cut refusal, source release before actual next GC under proved future coverage, target retirement race, W<R scan, error/source/destination/stage relocation and late native writes; test map multiple restores and original fill/effect boundaries.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Reuse existing QNT temporal work/unknown/retirement and Lean root-slot/alias/accounting owners with unchanged scope. Error ordering, C callback settlement, actual roster inclusion and generated root adapters remain source/native premises; a causal source chain is not native execution or another theorem.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A matched request NOOP is not proof pending effects were delivered. Cleared FOREIGN fields can coexist with an unknown callback result; retry can silently do nothing or duplicate effects from saved fields. Native list membership is not RootTask coverage. Requiring next GC DONE before source ACK can create a needless exit/GC wait cycle; dropping source before target coverage creates a missed-root prefix.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeFailure;
  ref part :>> entrySite=bulkPendingErrorProducer;
  ref part :>> exitSite=bulkTargetScanChain;
 }
 part bulkParkExitRefinement:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="bulkParkExitRefinement";
  attribute :>> precondition="Actual bulk purpose retains registered endpoint/input roots and current VM/source lifetime; raw physical span is closed at a complete-root boundary; collective participation, Scheme hooks, foreign effects and error delivery are separate authorities";
  attribute :>> argument="POLL jumps to stack-limit handler, which builds an internal return frame and dispatches interrupt-handler; it can call Scheme handlers. sync-op-interrupt saves/reloads GVM state around service_sync_op. execute_sync_op_loop participates in combined VM operations including resize, then drains owner cleanup and may throw. lifecycle_drain invokes release_foreign. Current root_round_begin enumerates active PSTATE RC sources, register_rc refuses cross-source relinking, and lifecycle_handoff transfers still chains/accounting rather than arbitrary RC roots.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="GC-only bulk parking requires a real effect-restricted adapter, not reuse of POLL or service_sync_op by name. Keep required collective participation and active-bulk retirement exclusion; factor permitted memory/root work from deferred user/native effects and errors. Cooperative owner exit can use a fully installed span in an existing surviving RC source, with ACK and next-round membership before releasing original roots; a VM-owned native list alone is not scanned.";
  attribute :>> missing="Implement a real bulk lifecycle purpose and purpose-aware close/abort/resize dispatch; effect-restricted synchronization/restore and rooted pending-error state; bounded target preparation and authorized same-VM root copying/query/ACK. Existing roster has no orphan-root source and existing register_rc cannot reparent a block. Abrupt unknown owner stop and active frozen-roster transfer remain retained/unqualified.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Keep pending GC, resize, heartbeat/user and foreign-cleanup work together without callbacks inside physical copy or missed collective participation. Cover known cooperative exit, target reserve/refusal/lost ACK, current-round transfer refusal, future-round target scan, stale writer, unknown stop and cleanup refusal. Real map repeated restore/winding and original fill POLLs remain unchanged; generic C-to-Scheme callbacks keep their effect semantics.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Existing QNT owns publish/close/unknown/retirement interleavings and Lean owns canonical slot/alias laws. The C dispatcher/effect split, complete root materialization and source-transfer adapter are source/native obligations; no duplicate formal model or claim of proved GC-only execution or dead-owner progress.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="Calling service_sync_op can invoke a release callback after memory restoration; masking sync interrupts can strand a collective. Reparenting RC header or retaining native metadata outside active roster loses future root scans. Generic terminal activation release can discard pending stage effects. Unknown join does not establish data closure or permission to change membership.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeReentry;
  ref part :>> entrySite=bulkSyncDispatch;
  ref part :>> exitSite=collectionDomainRoster;
 }
 part bulkStagingAuthority:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="bulkStagingAuthority";
  attribute :>> precondition="Copy operation owns a registered typed RC span and an actual bulk-purpose lifetime record; owner/VM incarnation, source-domain epoch, exact roots pointer, immutable count, checked range, stage revision and exclusive writer are validated before any positive-index store";
  attribute :>> argument="alloc_rc_roots publishes FAL-initialized immutable-count cells and mark_rc scans them under a frozen claimed source. Existing store_rc_root admits positive indices only for SFUN ROOTED/ACTIVE records and borrow count one. root_writer_open is current-owner OPEN and nonjoined; root_task_publish freezes under the same source gate but has no bulk-span drain. rc_can_close rejects non-FAL cells/borrows/scan leases; unlink checks refcount and borrows, so a bulk owner reference must survive pending writes and queries. Terminal activation cleanup currently releases roots generically and cannot settle staged effects.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Reuse RC allocation/list/scanner and existing lifecycle ownership, with a real bulk writer purpose and explicit scan-valid park/settlement/retirement adapters. Do not set SFUN kind, treat borrow count as authority, reduce root_count to hide partial state, or create a parallel registry. Existing handoff receipt roles name the needed installation/stop/producer/scan/query/resume/retire facts.";
  attribute :>> missing="Implement bulk-purpose validation and noncollecting bounded source-gate writes, enroll/drain destination physical spans before freeze, publish stage readiness separately from list registration, provide known-stop settlement and checked last-user cleanup dispatch. Current source has neither bulk-purpose authorization nor safe generic partial-commit/late-writer recovery.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Cover register/fill/ready/write/unknown/settled/parked/resumed/retired boundaries; malformed purpose, wrong source/span/index/count, freeze races, relocation of source/destination/stage referents, lost results and stale helper writes must not grant access. Test ordinary exit, prewrite cancellation, already committed result, unknown native stop and lifecycle teardown; preserve real map multi-shot aliases and no new user callbacks inside a native move.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Reuse existing QNT publish/freeze/unknown/task/last-user slices and Lean typed-slot/alias/checked-accounting premises with their unchanged owners. Handoff declarations are required source facts, not a new temporal executor, proof or runtime receipt implementation.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A live RC node can still be freed when its last owner/borrow is released despite scan-valid slots; allocating a typed span does not give a bulk writer SFUN authority. Holding a source lock across GC creates a scanner wait cycle. A changing filled prefix cannot replace immutable root_count or make torn pointers scannable. Generic terminal abort can lose unresolved destination writes.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=typedStagingSource;
  ref part :>> exitSite=bulkStageCloseGuard;
 }
 part bulkBranchAliasRefinement:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="bulkBranchAliasRefinement";
  attribute :>> precondition="Producer target and generated artifact identities are separate evidence; selected module aliases are resolved by canonical object identity and typed offsets; native extension/ABI branches require explicit admission";
  attribute :>> argument="macro-case-target reads compilation-options target and defaults to C. The vector macro forms public/primitive names and C subvector/subvalues move bodies. Observed _std.c routes vector-copy! through POLL to the primitive memmove and fill through VECTORSET plus POLL; small-copy allocation roots operands before deriving bodies. Tcl registration passes proc to scheme_create_cmd, RC stores a vector payload, call pins the native identity then generated Scheme entry reloads its current payload. Function conversion separately selects static c-define host or platform-conditional RC trampoline; pointer/string conversions have distinct data ownership.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Concrete branch, direct-caller and alias chains replace mere token counts for these reviewed mechanisms. Checked-in generated C corroborates a selected C path but does not establish current producer/build equivalence. RC root_count spans are already initialized before registration and scanned, but their positive-index write policy is SFUN-specific, so rooted bulk staging requires a real owner/write adapter rather than pretending to be an SFUN.";
  attribute :>> missing="Implement canonical typed bulk spans, stage-root owner admission, direction-preserving progress and cut-aware publication/repair; prove current generated-build/FrameSpec consumers and actual native stop/cleanup. Verify real callback ABI/platform branches; arbitrary C address escape and cross-library nonlocal exits remain unsupported unless qualified.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Test same-object left/right/equal/zero copies, distinct objects with shared referents, source/destination/staging relocation between completed chunks, lost completion before/after destructive writes, and old helper access. Preserve map aliases across two restores and Tcl nested callback/delete/exception paths; static-host and supported dynamic closure branches are separately admitted with unchanged budgets.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Use existing Lean injective identity/slot rewrite premises for canonical equality and staging roots; existing QNT owns writer-close/work/last-user/unknown settlement. The directional overlap invariant and concrete C-to-model adapter remain source obligations; no duplicate state model or data theorem and no new native pass is inferred.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A numeric physical-address comparison after relocation can misclassify aliasing; retrying an unknown overlap chunk consumes overwritten input. A registered byte RC buffer has root_count zero and is not rooted staging. Allocating a typed span does not grant a non-SFUN writer permission. A dynamic trampoline unsupported on the selected CPU cannot be counted as a tested callback path.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=bulkTargetSelection;
  ref part :>> exitSite=typedStagingSource;
 }
 part bulkForeignWriteCustody:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="bulkForeignWriteCustody";
  attribute :>> precondition="Selected modules, macro instances and native extensions declare pointer layout, incoming-edge effects, callbacks and last use; source/destination roots precede metadata or staging allocation; no concurrent conflicting vector mutation is assumed safe merely from a GC permit";
  attribute :>> argument="The vector macro generator selects raw word memmove for vector and values, scalar setters for fill and a direction-aware setter fallback outside C. Small copy macros initialize new payloads. FFI POINTER extracts a FOREIGN native address rather than automatically borrowing a Scheme body; string conversion allocates RC byte storage. Tcl ClientData pins an RC record across callback entry but create_cmd writes a vector directly and arbitrary c-code is emitted verbatim. These paths require distinct typed access and publication contracts.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="One whole bulk/native writer adapter must replace implicit raw-span assumptions. Complete actual generated/callback consumers plus explicit native extension admission are required; repository matches do not attest arbitrary C code or authorize independent collection.";
  attribute :>> missing="Provide a noncollecting bulk metadata reservation, canonical source+offset identities and relocation-safe rooted staging/progress where recovery is promised. Couple physical mutation to edge commit and writer closure. Unknown memmove may leave partially written words; only known write-stop plus sufficient rooted input permits reconstruction before scan. Scope/gate lifetime, deletion/callback exceptions, published-object distinction and whole consumer evidence remain open.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Preserve vector-copy overlap directions, fill, zero and card boundaries, boxed values, private construction and mutable frame semantics. Exercise overflow before first write and after completed chunks, source/destination movement, late writers, callback deletion, conversion failure, borrowed root reload and unknown exits; restore map twice with alias and winding equality. Native PBT and matched work/peak evidence must use the actual generated C and declared extension set.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Consume existing QNT publish/freeze/borrow/unknown/task/retirement results only within their declared scope and existing Lean slot/alias/accounting data laws. Bulk overlap/progress and new barriers are unproved source/native obligations, not automatically established by those models or duplicated as QNT/Lean theorems.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A barrier on VECTORSET alone misses C memmove. Retrying a partially completed overlapping move can read already overwritten input. An RC lifetime pin is not a stopped raw reader; casting FOREIGN_PTR does not imply a Scheme-heap edge. A dirty log does not make a torn destination pointer scannable; a failed join is not permission to repair concurrently.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=boxedBulkMove;
  ref part :>> exitSite=tclCommandOwner;
 }
 part crossRegionIncomingEdges:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="crossRegionIncomingEdges";
  attribute :>> precondition="Collected regions C and epoch are explicit; all direct roots and incoming slots from outside C are covered, including generated, reflective, bulk and native access; writes and relocation have distinct authorities";
  attribute :>> argument="Actual map evaluates proc, recursive tail, then cons under let*. Generated SETCAR/SETCDR/VECTORSET/CLOSURESET and continuation field stores are direct stores; targ-apply-simp-generator disables its ssb-space hook. store_rc_root has source admission and locking, and mark_rc rewrites canonical cells, but neither establishes all mature or cross-region incoming edges. A retained wrapper shares frame/denv and can outlive the request. Root retention, incoming-slot repair and native pointer validity are different premises.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Coordinated VM cuts remain the candidate until complete incoming-edge and raw-access closure is supplied. Independent regional collection is conditional, not implied by local allocation, W/R separation, root locks or release stores. Sharing and age are independent: a shared mature graph may still admit minor-scan exclusion.";
  attribute :>> missing="Bind generated direct/CAS/bulk stores, frame reconstruction/reflection, RC/foreign borrowers and collector rewrites to one edge policy. Reserve metadata before mutation; close and drain enrolled writers before frozen scanning, or separately establish concurrent rescan. Keep unknown effects, source/target roots and last users in custody; relocation-stable dirty-source identity and promotion residual edges remain implementation requirements.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="One whole map callback captures reusable control, mutates a shared mature cell/frame toward young storage, retains it through RC/FFI and restores twice across GC with winding intact. Exercise store-versus-close, log overflow, successful/failed CAS, native park/reload, relocation of dirty sources and unknown exits. Compare a coordinated cut and only qualified independent cuts; refusal affects GC policy, not valid Scheme mutation.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Existing QNT cut/publication/work owners retain temporal obligations; existing Lean slot/alias owners retain data obligations. A regional remembered-set protocol outside those scopes remains OPEN rather than receiving duplicate theorems. Source/native gates require actual adapter and execution evidence.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="Log-before-store can be scanned before the later mutation; log-after-store can miss a concurrently closed cut. A wrapper copy does not isolate the environment. Pinning one outer object does not validate raw pointers to movable descendants. Unknown unmediated writer vetoes the affected cut, not automatically every independent domain.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=generatedReferenceStore;
  ref part :>> exitSite=rootScan;
 }
 part regionCollectionPartition:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="regionCollectionPartition";
  attribute :>> precondition="Collected physical regions and epoch are declared; all incoming references, active/frozen root sources and native access are covered; copy and restore intervals are separately reserved";
  attribute :>> argument="Current alloc_heap_ptr aliases a PSTATE memory field, CollectorWorker arena is a private destination, and root_round_begin builds a VM-bound source roster. These are three different concrete responsibilities, not an implemented per-context nursery or independent GC domain. Candidate context-local young allocation can retain a VM-wide cut and shared mature storage; a finer collection cut additionally needs complete remembered incoming slots or qualified access/promotion/pinning rules.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="VM-wide coordinated minor collection remains the existing candidate; independent local minor or request-private collection is an alternative with unresolved entry/escape/barrier obligations. W different from R is not proof of multiple independent collection domains.";
  attribute :>> missing="Modern C generator stores and all bulk/reflection/native writers need incoming-edge coverage, noncollecting barrier overflow/failure custody, promotion/capacity accounting and actual domain/root membership closure. Pinned/still/permanent regions remain explicitly scanned/reclaimed as their semantics require.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Keep sharing observations equal while varying allocation placement/root-worker assignment; cover cross-context young edges, promoted-to-young edges, retained continuations, parked native loans and unknown writers. Unsupported independent cuts must refuse without erasing the original roots/capacity debt.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Existing shared_heap_cut and work/retirement QNT own temporal protocol slices; existing Lean owns alias/data laws. Those checked scopes do not model arbitrary multi-domain interference or prove a new remembered-set implementation; the source premise remains OPEN.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="Collecting a local nursery misses a pointer stored in another nursery/global/native structure; interpreting a worker destination as a mutator allocation region can overlap live copy/restore storage. Unknown same-domain writer cannot be waived by a smaller worker count.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeRoster;
  ref part :>> entrySite=mutatorRegionPlacement;
  ref part :>> exitSite=collectionDomainRoster;
 }
}
